READING: for every h-invariant compensator X, <X F_N ^ F_N> is either the metric-free topological term (X=1) or identically zero.
A kinetic term F_N ^ *F_N needs a Hodge star, i.e. a metric-dependent operator that an action Int <X F^F> (X constant) cannot supply;
the MM-type extension therefore carries NO spin(N) gauge kinetic coefficient (ABSENT), consistent with the Krasnov-Percacci remark.
